{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet","id":492158,"title":"Homebrewed Primal Form Facet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-25T18:29:34-07:00","id":492158,"title":"Homebrewed Primal Form Facet","content":"I wrote this as an alternative to Father's Form, which I know is not to everyone's taste. It could be used to replace Father's Form entirely, or as an optional alternative Purity Facet of the Gift of Change used by the Pure. It has not been playtested, so use at your discretion, and I'd love to hear how it works out in play.<br /> <br /> <u>Primal Form (Purity)</u><br /> It is said that before the fall of Pangea, the Urshul form was something altogether more terrifying. When <i>Urfarah</i> was slain, Luna took some of the form\u2019s original power away from the People. With this Facet, the Uratha can recall that power, if only for a short time. The Pure tribes favor this Facet, claiming it to be the \u201ctrue\u201d Urshul form.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Uratha can activate this Facet once per scene when she shifts to Urshul form. For as long as she remains in Urshul form, the character causes Lunacy as though she were in Gauru, regenerates lethal damage as though she had spent Essence to heal, and her opponents cannot add the appropriate Skill to Defense against her attacks (in addition to the usual benefits of Urshul form). This added potency comes at a cost, however; she suffers a -3 penalty to all Resolve + Composure rolls to resist <i>Kuruth</i> or gain lucidity until she changes form. After a number of turns equal to her (Hishu) Stamina + Primal Urge, she must shift to a different form or fall to <i>Kuruth</i>. If the Uratha shifts to Urshul form when she enters <i>Wasu-Im</i>, she will instinctively activate this Facet at no cost, even if she has already used it during the scene.<br /> <br /> Using this Facet while not in the grips of <i>Kuruth</i> is a conscious choice to embrace the Uratha\u2019s primeval nature, and counts as a Breaking Point towards Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":".  Clairifying an ambiguity as pointed out by TerraBen 04-27-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T19:40:18-07:00","id":492212,"title":"","content":"... I actually kinda like this one. I'm alright with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T19:42:05-07:00","id":492214,"title":"","content":"If you shift to Gauru from this, does your counter for 'how long I can stay in this form' reset?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T19:50:40-07:00","id":492219,"title":"","content":"Thanks! The only thing that kind of worries me is it's potentially a lot of turns of denying your opponents their Skill to Defense if you activate Primal Form, shift to Gauru when your time is up, run out your time in Gauru, then enter <i>Wasu-Im</i> and use Primal Form instinctively. I don't <i>think</i> that should be too much of a problem, but I would like to hear feedback from anyone who tries it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T19:52:51-07:00","id":492221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=492214#post492214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you shift to Gauru from this, does your counter for 'how long I can stay in this form' reset?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does as currently written, but if that proves to be a problem it could be fixed with a bit of rewording.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's how I see it happening. Let's assume a starting character with 2 Stamina and 1 Primal Urge. She shifts to Urshul and activates Primal Form. After 3 turns, she shifts to Gauru, ending the Facet. She remains in Gauru for 3 turns, then opts not to change form at the end of her Gauru time limit, giving her 1 more turn of Gauru, then she has to roll Resolve + Composure. If she fails, she goes straight to <i>Basu-Im</i>. If she succeeds, she shifts to Dalu or Urshul and enters <i>Wasu-Im. </i>If she shifts to Urshul, she instinctively activates Primal Form again. After 3 turns, she falls to <i>Basu-Im</i>, since she's in <i>Wasu-Im</i> and therefore can't change form to end the Facet, which sends her further into <i>Kuruth</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-25-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:37:37-07:00","id":493696,"title":"","content":"It's a cool Gift. I'd add an &quot;in addition to the usual benefits of the Urshul form&quot; or something to it. As written*, it could be unclear whether these add to the form or overwrite it.<br /> It seems like the anti-defense power wouldn't help when fighting spirits. Being as taking out wayward spirits was a large part of Urfarah's job, perhaps their defense can be halved.<br /> <br /> About the fluff: If Luna stripped the power down, why are the Pure better able to get that power back? Isn't the general idea about the Pure that they're pure because they've turned their back on any help Luna might offer? Maybe just say &quot;some of the power of this form faded&quot; rather than that Luna took it.<br /> <br /> *On a totally side note, does RAW mean &quot;rules as written&quot;? I've seen the phrase around a lot but only recently realized that I wasn't sure what it meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:05:34-07:00","id":493714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=492221#post492221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does as currently written, but if that proves to be a problem it could be fixed with a bit of rewording.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's how I see it happening. Let's assume a starting character with 2 Stamina and 1 Primal Urge. She shifts to Urshul and activates Primal Form. After 3 turns, she shifts to Gauru, ending the Facet. She remains in Gauru for 3 turns, then opts not to change form at the end of her Gauru time limit, giving her 1 more turn of Gauru, then she has to roll Resolve + Composure. If she fails, she goes straight to <i>Basu-Im</i>. If she succeeds, she shifts to Dalu or Urshul and enters <i>Wasu-Im. </i>If she shifts to Urshul, she instinctively activates Primal Form again. After 3 turns, she falls to <i>Basu-Im</i>, since she's in <i>Wasu-Im</i> and therefore can't change form to end the Facet, which sends her further into <i>Kuruth</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you just change to Dalu at the end of the third turn in Primal Form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:06:36-07:00","id":493716,"title":"","content":"Yep, it means rules as written. Contrast RAI (rules as intended).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I could repeat that definition in my sleep. Years spent on the CO boards for D&amp;D 3.5 does that to you.)</span><br /> <hr /><br /> Otherwise, this is pretty nice. I think the timer issue can be handled by having Gauru and PrimalForm!Urshul share a timer. So shifting into Gauru won't help, since both are running of white hot rage-juice (delicious, delicious rage-juice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:57:29-07:00","id":493749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493714#post493714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Couldn't you just change to Dalu at the end of the third turn in Primal Form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? The wording in the <i>Wasu-Im</i>?section made it sound to me like which ever form you pick, you're stuck in that form for the whole <i>Wasu-Im</i>. But I could see reading it as meaning you're limited to Urshul and/or Dalu (or Urhan and/or Hishu if you've got Controlled Burn). If that's the case, you can't reset the timer on Primal Form by shifting to Dalu and then back to Urshul in <i>Wasu-Im</i>, because the instinctive activation only triggers at the start of <i>Wasu-Im</i>. That's the intent, anyway. I'm of course open to feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:14:03-07:00","id":493755,"title":"","content":"I still kinda feel that you could just have it run off the Gauru timer; maybe treat turns spent in Primal Form as turns spent in Gauru? I think that would end up being cleanest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:19:13-07:00","id":493761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493696#post493696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a cool Gift. I'd add an &quot;in addition to the usual benefits of the Urshul form&quot; or something to it. As written*, it could be unclear whether these add to the form or overwrite it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, I will edit the original post to clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493696#post493696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the anti-defense power wouldn't help when fighting spirits. Being as taking out wayward spirits was a large part of Urfarah's job, perhaps their defense can be halved.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to be a slightly tonned-down version of Gauru's Primal Fear ability. I took out the auto-Down-and-Dirty and left in the defense nerf. The idea I was going for is that where Father's Form takes away some of Gauru's weaknesses at the cost of reducing its strengths and a potential Break towards Flesh, Primal Form would give the next-biggest form some of Gauru's strengths at the cost of also accepting some of its weaknesses and a potential Break towards Spirit. Feel free to make changes as you like if you use it in your own game, I'm just explaining the reasoning behind the choices I made with it to help inform your own homebrewing choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493696#post493696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the fluff: If Luna stripped the power down, why are the Pure better able to get that power back? Isn't the general idea about the Pure that they're pure because they've turned their back on any help Luna might offer? Maybe just say &quot;some of the power of this form faded&quot; rather than that Luna took it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff is carried over from the 1e version, where it was the fifth dot of Mother Luna's Gift instead of the Purity Facet of the Gift of Change, but it was specifically mentioned as the Pure's preferred form for hunting Uratha (as a side note, that's another reason I think not being as useful against spirits is fine, since it's actually meant more to use against other Werewolves). I figure the Pure see it as stealing back the power that Luna unjustly took away from them. And as with anything that references the myth of Wolf and Moon, it's a myth told entirely by oral tradition, so it not only could be wrong, it's <i>most likely</i> wrong, but the Uratha accept that because the symbolic truth is more important to them than the literal truth. That's my take, anyway, feel free to refluff for your own uses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493696#post493696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*On a totally side note, does RAW mean &quot;rules as written&quot;? I've seen the phrase around a lot but only recently realized that I wasn't sure what it meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, RAW is rules as written, and RAI is rules as intended. I also like to add a third RAF, meaning rules as fun, and stressing the fact that what you and your group finds fun is at least as important than what's written in the book and how the writers/developers intended the rule to work, if not moreso.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-27-2015, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:52:01-07:00","id":493791,"title":"","content":"Thanks for clarifying your thought process. I had forgotten where exactly it came from in 1st edition. I do remember that one of the facets of it was that it was bigger than Urshul usually is. Is that something you'd want to put back in?<br /> <br /> On a forum-format note, I've recently found that if you post quotes with quotation marks in them, it comes out with the code form ( &amp;quot; ) instead of the character (&quot;). Hitting the &quot;Edit&quot; button and then saving without changing anything fixes them back to the proper characters but doesn't label your post as edited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:30:55-07:00","id":493949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet?p=493791#post493791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for clarifying your thought process. I had forgotten where exactly it came from in 1st edition. I do remember that one of the facets of it was that it was bigger than Urshul usually is. Is that something you'd want to put back in?.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e version actually gave you a 6th form, which gave +4 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +4 Stamina, +3 Size, +3 Species factor, -3 Manipulation (+7 Health, +6 Initiative, +9 Speed) +3L grappling bites, +2L Claws, 2/1 armor, auto-heal 1 lethal each turn, and -3 on rolls to resist Death rage. As compared to normal Urshul, that's +2 Strength, +2 Stamina, +2 Size, +1 damage on teeth and claws, and the armor. It bordered on overpowered even as a 5th-dot Gift, so I thought it would be way too much for a 2E Facet, which are supposed to be worth roughly 3-dots (keeping in mind that the baseline is a bit higher in 2e). That's why I modeled it after Father's Form instead of the original Primal Form. I figured the added abilities were more important than the stat boosts, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}